{"id": "EUVD-2026-86164", "enisaUuid": "ee1e244a-9971-3c90-a71f-63c2ac3b0ca7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: embed f2fs_gc_kthread in f2fs_sb_info\n\nInstead of allocating f2fs_gc_kthread dynamically, embed it in\nf2fs_sb_info. This simplifies lifetime management and prepares for\nfixing race conditions during teardown.\n\n- __sbi_store\t\t\t- remount|shutdown\n\t\t\t\t - f2fs_stop_gc_thread\n - access sbi->gc_thread\n\t\t\t\t  - sbi->gc_thread = NULL\n - access sbi->gc_thread->f2fs_gc_task", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc004a1107e2c44cbdd2f1b1c2c85d32adc8f731", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ee6be9ee7f9a803e0f539af26ab1154fdde48ba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23eee01c732ec8c62b05416a05f0f88129df2960", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/99d14d61aa8beb6cb9a984b9fcddd45e35b24494", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d7bca9d583793bb7d0bac0d95a24ddd2e129eed"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93285", "GHSA-g7j3-cmg6-483m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08381150-91a9-37fe-84ec-e8a6f35e6b00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "13d68fe3-916a-330e-8f9c-e4134b17134a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "189871e8-d54d-38c2-a636-dca439417437", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "20722c7e-5490-3ee0-ad6b-bbbdee2f8d61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7950e9ac638e84518fbdd5c930939ad46a1068c5 <99d14d61aa8beb6cb9a984b9fcddd45e35b24494"}, {"id": "4628f053-5a94-3799-8426-c54a242ea129", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "520c3912-a234-33c5-996d-61d822347e0e", "product"